  <model metaid="meta_apixaban_liver" id="apixaban_liver" name="Model for hepatic apixaban metabolism." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for hepatic apixaban metabolism.</p>
        <p>The unbound apixaban in plasma equilibrates with the hepatocytes and is
metabolized by CYP3A4/5 (<code>API2M_k</code>, activity <code>f_cyp3a4</code>) to O-demethyl
apixaban (M2, fraction <code>f_m2</code>) and hydroxy apixaban (M7). M2 is sulfated to
M1. M1 and M7 are exported into the plasma, M1, M2 and M7 are excreted with
the bile into the intestinal lumen.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
